MISSION: PD_RUNTIME_REACHABILITY_PROOF_V1

Problem:
INPUT_CLICK_FOCUS_PROOF_V1 build/spawn/fault gates pass, but runtime proof is pending because QEMU test window only reaches PD1. This blocks live proof for silk-shell PD3 and sexinput PD4.

Goal:
Find why scheduler/runtime only reaches PD1 during the QEMU test window, and prove PD3 silk-shell + PD4 sexinput execute enough to emit runtime markers.

BACKUP BEFORE CHANGES.
If something goes wrong: READ HANDOUTS and .mds first.
Reduce token waste: rg first, inspect small snippets only, no broad dumps.
Save recurring fixes/issues in docs/handoff.

NO Linux assumptions. NO POSIX.
Strict no_std Rust Sex Microkernel.
PDX only. MPK/PKU/PKEY isolation.
No kernel/ABI/sex-pdx edits unless STOP FIRST.
No sex-pdx ABI edits unless STOP FIRST.
sexdisplay sole framebuffer writer.
Preserve framebuffer bounds checks.
No shared-memory/backing-buffer redesign.
No broad refactor.

Scope:
Investigate runtime reachability/scheduling/proof timing only.

Allowed inspection:
kernel/src/scheduler.rs
kernel/src/init.rs
kernel/src/interrupts.rs using docs/INTERRUPTS_QUICKMAP.md discipline
servers/sexinput/src/main.rs
servers/silk-shell/src/main.rs
scripts/runtime or gate scripts if relevant
docs/handoff/*.md

Do NOT read all of kernel/src/interrupts.rs.
Use:
rg "timer_interrupt_handler|switch_to|tick|enqueue|PD|fault.kill|faulted_task_halt|send_eoi|STATE_" kernel/src/interrupts.rs kernel/src/scheduler.rs kernel/src/init.rs -n
Then inspect only small sed ranges.

Task:
1. Determine whether PD3/PD4 are:
   - spawned but not scheduled
   - scheduled but not running long enough
   - running but markers not flushed/captured
   - blocked in pdx_listen
   - faulted/exited silently
   - starved by PD1 loop/yield behavior
   - missed by test window timeout
2. Add minimal proof markers if necessary:
   - scheduler.pd.pick id=N
   - scheduler.pd.enter id=N
   - pd3.alive
   - pd4.alive
   - pd3.listen.wait or pd3.loop.tick
   - pd4.listen.wait or pd4.loop.tick
3. Prefer diagnostic markers over behavior changes.
4. If a behavior fix is needed, make the smallest safe diff.
5. STOP FIRST if fix requires scheduler ABI redesign, kernel/userspace ABI change, or broad task model change.

Proof required:
- ./scripts/entrypoint_build.sh PASS
- SPAWN_GATE PASS
- FAULT_GATE PASS
- serial shows PD3 and PD4 runtime markers
- no #PF/#GP/panic
- docs/handoff/PD_RUNTIME_REACHABILITY_PROOF_V1.md updated

Output:
1. root cause
2. exact minimal diff
3. marker chain proving PD1, PD3, PD4 all execute
4. build/fault/spawn result
5. remaining risks
